    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d285">

                <pb facs="0545" n="517" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v03/pg517"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">353/10–2953: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Mission at the United
                        Nations</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d285-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1953-10-29T18:23:00-05:00">October 29,
                            1953—6:23 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p> Gadel 48. Re ICJ election. While you should not campaign against election of
                    Kozhevnikov, who we assume will receive widest support in view sentiment in
                    favor election of judges of Big Five to ICJ, you should not vote for him in SC
                    or GA but should abstain.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dulles</hi>
                    </signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d285-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d285-f1-content">
                <p>Drafted by Jones (UNP) and concurred in by Deputy Assistant SecretarySandifer,
                    cleared with the Bureau of European Affairs and L/UNA, approved for transmission
                    by Popper, and signed by Assistant Secretary Murphy.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
